Integrated wiring knowledge: the difference between LSZH and PVC
LSZH may be a halogen-free material, non-toxic, with good flame retardancy but poor mechanical properties. PVC may be a halogen-containing (chlorine) material, which is flammable and produces intense and harmful gases when burned, but it’s better mechanical properties.
