(1) Clean and maintain for the floor after laying/before use
Clean up the dust and debris on the floor surface first.
After washing with clean water, soaking dry, it can be used directly without waxing.
Wet mopping. (Dilute with neutral floor cleaner 1:20 with water, and mop the floor with a semi-wet mop.)
Dilute with strong dewaxing water 1:10 and spread it evenly on the ground, wait for 5-10 minutes, clean and dewax at low speed with a floor scrubbing machine and red grinding pad. Use a water suction machine to suck up the sewage in time.
Wash with clean water and blot dry until there is no residual detergent on the floor.
1. Greasy stains: For local oil stains, pour the stock solution of the water-based degreaser directly on a towel to wipe; for large areas of oil stains, dilute the water-based degreaser at a ratio of 1:10, and then clean it with a mopping machine and a red grinding pad at low speed.
Black offset printing: use a cleaning agent with a low-speed polishing machine and a white polishing pad to polish. For long-time black offset printing, you can pour the strong black offset remover directly on the towel and wipe it.
