Amniotic fluid is essential for life, it is necessary for the fetus to develop in the womb. However, when amniotic fluid is abnormally produced in excess or on the contrary, a deficit, can produce negative consequences in pregnancy, both for the mother and for the baby.
During pregnancy, the amniotic fluid changes in its quantity. In the beginning, usually until the fifth month, the fluid is increasing, being able to reach the liter towards the 30th or 31st week of gestation.
Which means that it only occurs in very rare cases and can be easily detected on ultrasound scans. Thus it is very important to go to all reviews of pregnancy, because only then can it be verified that the development is correct and, if not, act as necessary to avoid more serious complications.
