Food is a key element when caring for pregnancy and ensure that the fetus develops optimally. The Mediterranean diet is perfect when it comes to ensuring that the baby receives the nutrients it needs and the gestation process is adequate.
1 What are the benefits of the Mediterranean diet in pregnancy?
What are the benefits of the Mediterranean diet in pregnancy?
Several studies have indicated that the Mediterranean diet reduces the risk of the baby can get allergies.
There are a number of foods that belong to the Mediterranean diet and that should be consumed during the gestation process:
It is a product that is rich in monounsaturated fats and vitamin E. It is highly beneficial, especially when it comes to heart health. Vegetables and vegetables should be present in the diet of any pregnant woman.
The fruit provides a good amount of vitamins, minerals and fiber. Being rich in water, its intake is perfect for pregnant women to be well hydrated.
Cereals and their derivatives cannot be missing from the diet of pregnant women.
Dairy products and their derivatives provide a good number of nutrients to the body such as proteins, minerals and vitamins. As with fish, special care must be taken with some cheeses that are not well fermented and can cause problems for both the woman and the fetus.
