Have you dared to create a urban garden on your terrace following our advice?
If so, it's time to start planting and see some plants grow like these vegetables to plant in May that we propose today.
The five vegetables The ones we are talking about today are a good alternative for beginners. They will keep you entertained and allow you to bring fresh food to the table without having to go shopping.
Furthermore, it is not convenient for the minimum temperatures to fall below 10 degrees if we want them to develop correctly. And that, at least here in the north, has not happened to date.
To the aubergines they like the heat that is why they are grown during the summer. And they are demanding with the hours of light they require to develop properly, between 10 to 12 hours a day, so you will need to choose a sunny spot in the garden or terrace for them.
They require frequent and abundant watering, but be careful not to flood their roots!
Courgettes are also hungry crops: once they have started to flower they need to be fertilized frequently. Harvesting is usually carried out about 90 days after planting, when the fruits of the plant are not yet fully ripe.
It is essential to plant them in well-draining soil about 25 centimeters apart from each other and water them lightly frequently to keep the soil slightly moist at all times. As for the place, it should be in a relatively cool place, where it avoids the sun in the middle of the day.
Cherry tomatoes need sun and heat for their fruits to ripen, which is why they are usually planted in late spring. The temperature should not fall below 10ºC and it is convenient around 20ºC for the seedlings to develop properly.
They like to receive sun all day as well as clay soil, well aerated and rich in humus. This must be always slightly moistAlso, if you want them to run smoothly.
Would you like to enjoy the relaxed atmosphere that beach houses transmit all year round?
The choice of colors is key to achieving that bright and relaxed atmosphere that makes us feel so good in beach houses. Choose a neutral base that has white as the protagonist and uses other natural tones such as wood as a complement is always a good choice.
Apply this color to textiles to achieve a subtle touch of color, opting for a single shade or a combination of several.
