Is my cat sick?
How can I tell if my cat is sick?
So we do get to worry more than necessary. So, today we leave you with some clues with which you will start suspect that something is happening And as such, you need to go to the vet as soon as possible to completely remove your doubts.
1 Changes in your appetite
Changes in your appetite
For example, they are very clean but if you notice that it is not cleaned as before or perhaps, it goes to the other extreme and its cleaning is excessive, it will already give us a clue that something is happening.
Perhaps at this point it is difficult to know if my cat is sick, because they sleep, they sleep a lot of hours. But if you notice that he still spends more time than usual with his eyes closed, if you also notice that he tries to hide or that he wakes up very listless, something is wrong.
Hence if you notice a drastic, almost sudden change, it may be that it is alerting us to something behind it. If he doesn't want to play, if he's a bit listless, he may have some kind of respiratory problem.
