The most appropriate thing is to let it dry in the open air so as not to abuse the heat tools. But if you have a lot of hair or frizzy hair, letting it dry can complicate the task of straightening.
Once the hair is completely dry, run your hands through the most hidden areas to make sure you remove all the moisture, it is necessary to detangle the hair very well. Brush with damp hair to detangle as much as possible, and go back to brush dry hair before straightening.
Always start by passing the iron from the root to the middle of the hair's length, pass about 3 times to leave this area that generally has more curl very smooth. From medium to ends you will only need one or two passes, do not abuse the tips and you will prevent them from drying outopen and have to cut too often.
A very important reminder and that for a long time we have done the other way around, the serum is an oil and should not be applied before the straightening, if not after. Think of the kitchen, when you use oil to cook hot it burns with the heat, on the contrary when you use it raw, you hydrate the food.
