From the Valdecea car park there are about 1000 meters to the esplanade of the hermitage, and to make this route you have two options. You can follow the River Path, which involves overcoming some small difficulty such as crossing the river over stepping stones, or continuing along the forest track, a walk that can be done even with sandals and baby strollers.
It has 25 pedestrian itineraries of different length and difficulty that pass through the most interesting places in the Natural Park. Within the park you can also visit the hermitage inside the Santa Margarita volcano, the Coscat volcano museum space or the old town of Sant Pau.
The Martos olive grove is located in Jaén, in the municipality of the same name that, sheltered by its Rock, provides them with an optimal microclimate and very fertile soil. The more than 20.000 hectares of its municipal area are conquered by the monoculture of the olive grove and, especially, by the scenic beauty that its majestic centenary olive trees.
The enclave is located just over a kilometer from the Marteño town center, next to the road that connects Martos with Santiago de Calatrava (J-213). At kilometer 1,3 you will find the first indication of the Centennial Olive Trees and, as soon as you pass some agrarian buildings, you will find the second indication.
On the border between Burgos and the Basque Country is the highest waterfall on the peninsula: the Nervión waterfall. This great waterfall of 270 meters of altitude located in the Monte de Santiago protected area, is a spectacle of nature that we cannot always enjoy.
In just 2 km on foot you will reach the spectacular viewpoint over which this spectacular waterfall can be seen rushing. Another route to see the Nervión waterfall from its upper part is the one that starts from the town of Untzaga in the province of Alava.
In the northern valleys of Cáceres, in the region surrounding Hervás, is held every fall between October and December Magic Fall, an initiative that makes the pleasure of enjoying nature and the rural charms of the place even more attractive. Hence, it is one of the natural enclaves that we have chosen to visit in November.
Don't you want to go on an excursion or prepare a rural getaway to one of these natural enclaves?
