It is a modern type of high-tech communication that allows you to use your phone over the Internet or any other IP network to make calls, video communication, international and long distance faxes in real time.
IP telephony stands for a set of communication protocols, VoIP equipment, software, technologies, and methods that provide powerful, non-traditional telephone communication functions.
To learn more about IP telephony, stay with us here. We will show you the difference between IP and analog telephony, how it works, its advantages, costs and how to hire the service.
The difference between IP and analog telephony is the lack of a cable and a traditional telephone, which are used by analog telephony. Instead, for the organization of telephone communication through IP networks, special equipment is used as IP telephony gateways.
In case the call reaches a normal telephone, the signal passes through an IP gateway which converts a digital signal (VoIP) into an analog one. The same happens when making calls through IP telephony to mobile phones.
Upon reaching the recipient's address, the transmitted information is decoded again, acquiring the format of the usual voice signal. All of this happens in a matter of fractions of a second, in real time with no loss of transmission quality.
It can be accessed virtually regardless of geographic location. You only need high-speed Internet access
Confidentiality and security. Thanks to encrypted communication channels, access to information by third parties is closed
Optimal solution. Offices, companies and organizations benefit thanks to its versatility, it allows you to make the most of communication without making any effort.
By using VOIP telephony, the difference in prices compared to analog communication can be clearly seen. Calls are not charged within the networkThat is, subscribers using the services of an IP telephony provider communicate using software or hardware, saving money.
