The House on Thursday passed a short-term stopgap measure that keeps the government open for another two weeks. The Senate is expected to pass the spending bill this week.
Among market participants, there is optimism that the tax cuts will boost growth and lead markets to rethink how aggressively the Federal Reserve could raise rates in 2018, said Kit Juckes, a strategist at Société Générale, in a note to investors.
Gold prices fell to four-month lows on Thursday pressured by continued dollar strength on the back of investor optimism over the progress of US tax reform.
Oil prices settled higher on Thursday as a threatened strike in Nigeria and growing Middle East political tensions stoked fears of supply disruptions, while ongoing OPEC-led output curbs supported sentiment.
