Euro weakness, meanwhile, added to dollar strength, amid an uptick in political tension in the region after the Spanish government said Catalan authorities must end a bid for independence by Thursday.
Equities entered the session trading in record territory, with the Nasdaq and S&P notching record closes on Tuesday.
In economic news, housing starts jumped 8.3 percent last month, hitting their highest level since February. Mortgage applications, meanwhile, rose 6.3 percent.
