Oil prices were firm buoyed by data showing a fall in U.S. crude inventories and by record car sales in the United States.
The dollar was almost unchanged against the other major currencies in subdued trade on Thursday, as markets showed no reaction to the release of disappointing U.S. jobless claims data.
