A healthy sebum film is the first element of healthy, brighter skin. The sebum membrane has important physiological functions on the skin and even the whole body, mainly in the following aspects:
The sebum film is the most important layer of skin moisture retention, which can effectively lock moisture, prevent excessive evaporation of skin moisture, and prevent a large amount of external moisture and certain substances from infiltrating. As a result, the weight of the skin remains normal.
The pH of the sebum membrane is between 4.5 and 6.5, which is weakly acidic. This weak acidity enables it to inhibit the growth of microorganisms such as bacteria and has a self-purifying effect on the skin, so it is the immune layer on the skin surface.
Excessive sebum secretion can cause oily, rough skin, enlarged pores, and prone to acne problems. Too little secretion can lead to dry skin, scaling, lack of luster, aging, etc.
If the sebum membrane is too thin, then the skin will be more sensitive to external stimuli. An image will be shot under the cross-polarized light and based on this image Meicet system uses an algorithm to get 3 images- sensitivity, red area, heatmap.
