Is 304 stainless steel the same as food grade 304 stainless steel?Not the same! Food grade and brand, belong to two systems, but there are countless links.
The name of the old NATIONAL standard GB 9684 is the National Standard for Food Safety stainless Steel Products. This national standard has been replaced in 2017 by GB 4806.9-2016 National Standard for Food Safety metallic Materials and Products used in Food Contact (this new standard combines the original two national standards applicable to stainless steel (GB 9684) and aluminum (GB 11333)).
In this NATIONAL standard, the provision of a migration test, put stainless steel materials into a simulated food solution (generally acidic solution) for immersion, after reaching the specified time test whether there are certain elements in the solution, as shown in the following table
We are in the purchase of tableware (actually said “tableware” is not quite standard, should be “stainless steel contact food”), should mainly see its packaging has “GB4806.9-2016″ words, only through the detection of products, we can rest assured to buy.
